kmsro, dril: sgx as a render-only GPU

kmsro pairs a KMS-only display device with the SGX545 under powervr_sgx: a
scanout buffer is a dumb buffer of the display device, imported into the
GPU.

powervr_sgx is a PCI device (the CE5300's SGX is its own PCI function;
Cedarview's sits behind gma500's), so a platform display device such as
simpledrm on a boot framebuffer has to find its render node off the
platform bus: render nodes of PCI devices are taken when their driver is
powervr_sgx.

An X server's GLX (AIGLX) loads <display driver>_dri.so: dril stubs for
simpledrm and sgx.

